eterization for the scaled sequence.\n\n   - Anneal tau from 10 to 500, for example.\n\n   - The optimization candidate: a theta (log scaling which corresponds to coefficients).\n\n5. **Gradient evaluations**:\n\n   - use finite-differences gradient for scalability.\n\n   - but simpler: rely on the provided analytic gradient for smoothed_max in `smoothed_obj_and_grad`.\n\n6. **Time checks**:\n\n   - use `time.monotonic()` to track progress.\n\n   - call evaluate_sequence when final candidate is ready.\n\n   - main strategy: continuous optimization until either a candidate with <= 2 <= 1.506 objectives is found, and time runs out.\n\n   - fallback to worst candidate if improvement not found within time.\n\n7. **Interface with evaluate_sequence**:\n\n   - the final candidate after retrieve will be normalized and then evaluated.\n\n   - we compare the objective only after all processing: the search function may propose a sequence of coefficients that are not the final output.\n\nImplementation Details:\n\n- The sequence structure investigations must have length 800.\n\n- Optimization: multi-start version of the previous program's smoothed optimization.\n\nRepresentations:\n\n- Use numpy arrays for sequencen and convolve is built-in.\n\n- But always keep the sequence dimension (length).\n\n- The normalized sequence a has sum=1.\n\n- The objective function computes max_b over the convolution.\n\nSearch Choices:\n\n- remix parent sequence by shifting distribution boundaries.\n\n- have different initializations:\n\n  1. Original parent: we know only partially, but we can sample and adjust.\n\n  2. Log-normal distributed ones: likely not.\n\n  3. Gaussian-like boundaries: but non-negative.\n\n  4. Mix of boundaries and uniform gaps.\n\nCompute Budget:\n\n- time=1500 seconds.\n\n- plenty time for gradient calculations and first-principal validation.\n\n  **  all intellectual steps carefully defined and ready to be implemented by the assistant after this handoff.**",
